# Maximum

```python
df.groupby("Department")["Salary"].max()
```

### Meaning

```text
Find Highest Value in Each Group
```

Example:

```text
50000
60000

Highest = 60000
```

### Memory

```text
max()
↓
Highest Value
```

---

# Minimum

```python
df.groupby("Department")["Salary"].min()
```

### Meaning

```text
Find Lowest Value in Each Group
```

Example:

```text
50000
60000

Lowest = 50000
```

### Memory

```text
min()
↓
Lowest Value
```

---

# Multiple Aggregations Using agg()

```python
df.groupby("Department").agg({
    "Salary":["mean","max","min"]
})
```

### Meaning

```text
Group By Department
↓
Calculate

Average
Highest
Lowest

Together
```

Output:

```text
            Salary
             mean   max   min

HR          42500 45000 40000
IT          55000 60000 50000
```

### Memory

```text
agg()
↓
Many Calculations Together
```

---

# Pivot Table

```python
pivot = df.pivot_table(
    values="Salary",
    index="Department",
    aggfunc="mean"
)
```

### Meaning

```text
values
↓
Column To Calculate

index
↓
Group By Column

aggfunc
↓
Calculation
```

Read As:

```text
Take Salary
↓
Group By Department
↓
Find Average
```

### Memory

```text
pivot_table()
↓
Summary Report
```

---

# Custom Aggregation Function

### Create Function

```python
def range_func(x):
    return x.max() - x.min()
```

### Use Function

```python
df.groupby("Department")["Salary"].agg(range_func)
```

### Example

```text
IT

50000
60000
```

Calculation:

```text
60000 - 50000

= 10000
```

Output:

```text
Department

IT    10000
HR     5000
```

### Memory

```text
Custom Function
↓
My Own Calculation
```

